id: pm-1w3ljt
title: "GH-663: fresh init must install and surface the semantic merge fence"
description: "Make the SDK-backed init lifecycle install the committed .gitattributes merge mappings and clone-local git driver configuration by default, preserve an explicit opt-out, and provide actionable recovery when a raw conflict reveals a missing fence."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:init","area:merge","area:sdk",gh-issue,multi-agent
created_at: "2026-07-24T12:38:27.541Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T17:01:28.003Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-24T13:35:02.738Z"
author: codex-root-agent
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Public SDK workspace-init primitives own a typed merge-fence policy; CLI init is a thin adapter with an explicit opt-out; fresh git repositories merge concurrent non-overlapping item/history edits without raw conflicts after init; status/read-only init paths do not mutate; missing-fence diagnostics give an exact recovery command; temporary packed-install tests cover custom tracker roots, worktrees/clones, opt-out, idempotence, and conflict recovery."
parent: pm-dj98
risk: high
confidence: high
release: v2026.7.25
reporter: codex-root-agent
severity: high
repro_steps: "Initialize a fresh git workspace with pm init, create divergent branch edits to one item, and merge without separately running pm merge install; raw item and history conflicts occur."
resolution: Fresh Git-backed init installs the semantic merge fence through public SDK primitives by default with explicit opt-out and read-only status behavior.
expected_result: "Fresh init establishes shared merge attributes and clone-local drivers by default, next steps explain per-clone setup, opt-out is explicit, and reconcile/validate guidance names pm merge install when the fence is absent."
actual_result: "Fresh init neither installs nor surfaces the merge fence, so the default multi-agent branch workflow hard-conflicts despite complete merge-driver machinery."
component: workspace initialization and semantic merge safety
regression: true
customer_impact: Agents following the default onboarding path can hit raw conflicts and lose the conflict-free multi-agent guarantee.
