comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T12:38:27.541Z",codex-root-agent,"Duplicate-check evidence: searched every status for GH-663, fresh init merge fence, .gitattributes, merge-driver installation, and multi-agent conflict recovery. Closed pm-g5sx/pm-iwsj own the shipped machinery and repo adoption; pm-hous owns ignore-file lifecycle. No item owns default fresh-init fence wiring, so this focused issue is canonical."
  "2026-07-24T12:40:40.798Z",codex-root-agent,"Implementation start: claimed as an actively worked part of the broad SDK workspace mutation integrity PR. TDD scope covers deterministic id allocation, atomic stale-lock takeover, init cache and merge-fence ownership, schema migration idempotency/recovery, cross-runtime machine channels, and the fixed 10k performance gate."
  "2026-07-24T13:35:01.779Z",codex-root-agent,"Completion evidence: final packed tarball in fresh Git repos proved default init installs .gitattributes and all clone-local driver definitions, agent-guidance=status leaves .gitignore/.gitattributes byte-identical, custom tracker roots render correct fence paths, and --no-merge-fence leaves .gitattributes absent. A real two-branch semantic merge preserved independent comments and notes on one item and storage_integrity returned ok. Full gate remains 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-07-24T13:48:59.731Z",codex-root-agent,"Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/673 (broad SDK workspace mutation and migration primitives)."
